WEBVTT

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:09.760
So we've set up our game so that when we
pick up the power up and then we collide with

00:00:09.761 --> 00:00:16.680
our enemy we should get a console statement
saying that we've collided with our enemy.

00:00:16.681 --> 00:00:18.736
Now we're going
to add a little bit of

00:00:18.748 --> 00:00:21.360
programming so that way
when we actually collide

00:00:21.635 --> 00:00:24.920
with the enemy they get sent flying away.

00:00:24.921 --> 00:00:27.814
In our player controller
script we're going

00:00:27.826 --> 00:00:30.800
to go down to our on
collision enter method.

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:32.755
Now since this is the
place where we actually

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:34.560
interact with our
enemy when they collide

00:00:34.709 --> 00:00:39.640
this will be the best place to be
able to do this entire interaction.

00:00:39.889 --> 00:00:42.534
Now in our if statement
for our collision we'll

00:00:42.546 --> 00:00:44.920
actually need our rigid
body for our enemy

00:00:44.921 --> 00:00:49.280
that way we can
actually apply forces to it.

00:00:49.281 --> 00:00:51.320
So we'll call it the enemy rigid body.

00:00:51.321 --> 00:00:54.971
So we set our rigid
body when we collide with

00:00:54.983 --> 00:00:58.320
our enemy we get its
game object and then

00:01:01.259 --> 00:01:04.710
we get the component
that we need in this case

00:01:04.722 --> 00:01:07.960
we need the rigid body
and then we actually

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:10.154
need to calculate
the direction that we're

00:01:10.166 --> 00:01:12.320
trying to go away from
the player so we need

00:01:13.399 --> 00:01:21.200
a vector 3 for that direction we'll just
call it away from player and to calculate

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.903
this we need to take
the enemy's current

00:01:34.915 --> 00:01:39.320
position and subtract it
by our current position.

00:01:39.321 --> 00:01:43.800
So now we know what direction the enemy is
coming in and what direction we should send

00:01:43.949 --> 00:01:49.400
it back by subtracting
by our current position.

00:01:50.499 --> 00:01:58.400
And then last but not least we're
going to apply a force to that rigid body.

00:01:58.401 --> 00:02:02.920
So we add a force.

00:02:02.921 --> 00:02:05.825
The direction we send
it to is in the direction

00:02:05.837 --> 00:02:08.320
of our vector 3 that
we set up away from

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:15.320
the player we'll multiply it by 10 just as
a random value and we want to make this an

00:02:15.345 --> 00:02:22.920
instant interaction so we're actually going
to use a force mode and use impulse so that

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.680
it applies the force immediately.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:34.560
Now after I've saved in Unity when I press
play for my game and I pick up this power

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:43.520
up you can see when I hit the enemy it gets
sent flying off in the opposite direction.

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:47.400
Last but not least we're going to
go into our player controller script.

00:02:47.401 --> 00:02:50.871
Now we're going to
create another variable just

00:02:50.883 --> 00:02:54.440
to hold the actual
strength of that interaction.

00:02:54.441 --> 00:02:56.225
So we're going to
make it private since 10

00:02:56.237 --> 00:02:58.120
was a pretty good number
maybe we make it 15

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:03.150
just to add a bit more
we'll make it a float and we'll

00:03:03.151 --> 00:03:12.040
call it power up strength
and we'll set it to 15.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.650
And then in our on collision
enter where we add the force

00:03:15.651 --> 00:03:20.680
and multiply it by 10 we'll
just use power up strength.

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:25.249
Now what you're going
to do is in the player

00:03:25.261 --> 00:03:29.120
controller script in on
collision enter inside

00:03:29.121 --> 00:03:31.456
of your if statement
you're going to add a

00:03:31.468 --> 00:03:34.040
line of code so that we
can get the rigid body

00:03:34.041 --> 00:03:36.903
of the enemy and
then you're going to add

00:03:36.915 --> 00:03:40.280
another line to get the
direction that we should

00:03:40.305 --> 00:03:44.184
send the enemy away
from the player and then

00:03:44.196 --> 00:03:48.000
you're going to apply
a force to that enemy

00:03:48.001 --> 00:03:50.993
in the direction away
from the player times

00:03:51.005 --> 00:03:54.080
our power up strength
variable and make sure

00:03:54.081 --> 00:03:59.240
that the force is applied instantly
using force mode dot impulse.

00:03:59.241 --> 00:04:00.241
Now it's your turn.